  "description": "Kula voyaging canoes of the Massim — Trobriands, Woodlark, Dobu and beyond — carry carved lagim prowboards: curving openwork cut scrollwork, mounted frigate-bird figures, zigzag turquoise-and-white geometric fills, topped by a bird or zigzag crest. The board faces the partner village at kula exchange; its ornament plus sago-paste charms and missile-deflecting magic promise safe passage and successful shell-armband and necklace trade. Prow aesthetics mark rank, lineage and sailing magic in one object.",
